        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Mention the Facebook Conteiner as a potential cause for failed CORS request]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40111</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40111"/>
        <updated>2025-06-27T18:12:57.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1126966?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">This pull request updates the documentation to mention the <strong>Facebook Container Firefox plugin</strong> as a potential cause for failed Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) requests that return <code class="notranslate">null</code>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The Facebook Container plugin can interfere with CORS requests, leading to <code class="notranslate">null</code> responses without clear indication of the cause. Adding this information will help users troubleshoot unexpected CORS failures more effectively, saving them time and effort.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">The Facebook Container is an official Firefox add-on designed to isolate Facebook-related activity. Its sandboxing behavior can impact network requests, including those related to CORS.</p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>nouai</name>
            <email>nouai@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/nouai</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2025-06-27T18:12:35.000Z</published>
    </entry>
