    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Fix: remove incorrect "form" attribute]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40097</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40097"/>
        <updated>2025-06-28T17:03:18.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38193798?u=51a29a96b848dcb858148a9940509bf1d87c682a&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Removed the incorrect <code class="notranslate">form</code> attribute on the <code class="notranslate">&lt;meter&gt;</code> element.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The <code class="notranslate">form</code> attribute on <code class="notranslate">&lt;meter&gt;</code> is not not mentioned in the spec and, to my knowledge, is not supported in any current browser implementation.</p>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-meter-element" rel="nofollow">HTML Living Standard – meter element</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">The only references to the <code class="notranslate">form</code> attribute on <code class="notranslate">&lt;meter&gt;</code> I could find are from W3C:</p>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/WD-html5-author-20110809/the-meter-element.html" rel="nofollow">www.w3.org | 4.10.17 The meter element — HTML5: Edition for Web Authors</a></p>
<p dir="auto">The page list <code class="notranslate">form</code> and says:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">The form attribute is used to explicitly associate the meter element with its form owner.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">But it does not list <code class="notranslate">name</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">On the w3schools website there is an example that uses both <code class="notranslate">form</code> and <code class="notranslate">name</code>:</p>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">&lt;meter id="anna" form="form1" name="anna" min="0" low="40" high="90" max="100" value="95"&gt;&lt;/meter&gt;</code></p>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://www.w3schools.com/tags/att_meter_form.asp" rel="nofollow">www.w3schools.com | HTML meter form Attribute</a></p>
<p dir="auto">The same page indicates the form attribute is <strong>Not supported</strong> in all browsers.</p>
<p dir="auto">My guess is this originated from a typo or misinterpretation in earlier W3C drafts.</p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>SB3NDER</name>
            <email>SB3NDER@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/SB3NDER</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2025-06-26T23:15:03.000Z</published>
    </entry>
