<p dir="auto">Mention that <code class="notranslate">canvas</code> needs <code class="notranslate">aria-label</code> rather than <code class="notranslate">alt</code>, and mention the use of <code class="notranslate">alt=""</code> to signal that an image is purely decorative.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">I'm new to <code class="notranslate">canvas</code> and was confused when  the accessibility checker complained but the linked section only mentioned <code class="notranslate">alt</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">The existing text mentions that a label is needed for contentful images, but doesn't say how to stop the checker complaining for images that aren't contentful.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">N/A</p>
